Z||000000||Fast Eddie||04-23-2001||07:37 PM||||I have an '85 notchback I would love to turn into a convertible. Where can I find some good info on how to do this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wade87GT||04-23-2001||08:57 PM||||I think you can still order a convert kit from the Fiero Owners Club of America (FOCOA) 1-714-917-2007   <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com/index.html</A> <BR>Check the link on their 17th Annual Fiero Festival, Williamsburg, Va. It's one one the biggest Fiero events of the year. I'm sure you'll see a few convertibles there. Also, don't forget to do a search right here at PFF on them too. Lots of info.<P>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||04-23-2001||09:23 PM||||There was just an e-mail on the Fiero Mailing list:<P>"Make an offer around $2500 for this Automada convertible kit.  Fits any year notchback Fiero.  Best you can buy for the Fiero.  Have all parts and instructions.  Need to sell in next 2 weeks.  When top is down it sits flush with the grills and deck lid, unlike some other bulky kits.  I live in St. Louis."<P>It was posted by  Scott Morris samorris@lycos.com<P>That's all the info I have on it.  You might drop him a note....<BR>||||reg||1
